Here is a MATLAB code that calculates the time difference between two dates with precision down to the millisecond and also takes into account time zones. The code is also capable of calculating the difference in business hours and excluding weekends and holidays:
```
function [time_diff, business_hours_diff] = time_difference(start_date, end_date, timezone)
% Convert dates to UTC time
start_date_utc = datetime(start_date, 'TimeZone', timezone, 'Format', 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.SSS');
end_date_utc = datetime(end_date, 'TimeZone', timezone, 'Format', 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.SSS');
% Calculate time difference in milliseconds
time_diff = milliseconds(end_date_utc - start_date_utc);
% Calculate business hours difference
business_hours_diff = 0;
while start_date_utc < end_date_utc
    % Exclude weekends and holidays
    if isweekend(start_date_utc) || ismember(start_date_utc, holidays())
        start_date_utc = start_date_utc + caldays(1);
        continue;
    end
    % Add business hour
    business_hours_diff = business_hours_diff + 1;
    start_date_utc = start_date_utc + hours(1);
end
end
function h = holidays()
% Define holidays
new_year = datetime('01-Jan-2022');
memorial_day = datetime('30-May-2022');
independence_day = datetime('04-Jul-2022');
labor_day = datetime('05-Sep-2022');
